# Unit_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Games with many discrete unit types (strategy_simulation).

## 2. This document owns
- Unit roster identity: role, movement class, attack pattern, counters/countered-by.
- Stat block schema (fields every unit fills) and cost curves.
- Upgrade/veterancy rules applied to units.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Combat resolution formulas — Gameplay/Economy systems.
- Faction availability — Faction_Design.
- AI behavior implementation — AI_Systems.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Roster philosophy / 2. Roles triangle / 3. Stat schema / 4. Roster table / 5. Cost curves / 6. Counters web / 7. Veterancy / 8. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Unit vs Enemy: fielded strategic pieces vs hostile actors; both may share AI archetypes.
- Counter relationships live here, not in faction lore.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every unit fills the full stat schema (or declared N/A).
- Counter web is consistent (no one-sided hard counters without cost justification).
